{"title":"Mock AIME 1 2007-2008 Problems/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_2007-2008_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Binomial_expansion\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Binomial expansion\">expansion</a> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/9/409a812e0f9801ede001b6a0d43f35fd1c46918d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x+1)^n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"63\" height=\"18\" /> has 3 consecutive terms with <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Coefficient\" title=\"Coefficient\">coefficients</a> in the ratio <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/8/e68657d9fca2085bb50dfd198a2a8c34b3d9f90e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1:2:3$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" /> that can be written in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/a/50a88dec97bf966a558ba3b7645a197e35537e1e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[{n\\choose k} : {n\\choose k+1} : {n \\choose k+2}\\]\" width=\"200\" height=\"53\" />\nFind the sum of all possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9ece7f97f556d5af63003cb94ecbc04def23999.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"42\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_2007-2008_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By definition, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/0/140d0491279ea8def90cd3380f9be2753167e35b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${n\\choose k} = \\frac{n!}{k!(n-k)!}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"143\" height=\"53\" />. The ratio of the first two terms give us that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/2/ab2611ca0c9789888b3ab9a8a60af94b0b8a1acb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}\\frac{1}{2} &amp;= \\frac{\\frac{n!}{k!(n-k)!}}{\\frac{n!}{(k+1)!(n-k-1)!}} = \\frac{k+1}{n-k}\\\\ 2&amp;=n-3k\\end{align*}\" width=\"208\" height=\"75\" />The ratio of the second and third terms give us that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/f/58fea6146851cd52932c6dbb825b080fc4348e95.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}\\frac{2}{3} &amp;= \\frac{\\frac{n!}{(k+1)!(n-k-1)!}}{\\frac{n!}{(k+2)!(n-k-2)!}} = \\frac{k+2}{n-k-1}\\\\ 8&amp;=2n-5k\\end{align*}\" width=\"239\" height=\"74\" />\nThis is a linear system of two <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Equation\" title=\"Equation\">equations</a> with two unknowns, indicating that there is a unique solution. Solving by substitution or multiplying the top equation and subtracting, we find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/7/817f2c3f9dd52d5f4be1204987fca8a154548cfc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = 4, n = 14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"104\" height=\"16\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/7/8b7c6a46cd64b2e66fc4e10e35e42166cac488bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+k=\\boxed{018}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"106\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_2007-2008_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_2007-2008\" title=\"Mock AIME 1 2007-2008\">Mock AIME 1 2007-2008</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_2007-2008_Problems\" title=\"Mock AIME 1 2007-2008 Problems\">Problems</a></b>, <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/viewtopic.php?t=196980\">Source</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_2007-2008_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"Mock AIME 1 2007-2008 Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_2007-2008_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"Mock AIME 1 2007-2008 Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_2007-2008_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"Mock AIME 1 2007-2008 Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_2007-2008_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"Mock AIME 1 2007-2008 Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_2007-2008_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"Mock AIME 1 2007-2008 Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_2007-2008_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"Mock AIME 1 2007-2008 Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_2007-2008_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"Mock AIME 1 2007-2008 Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_2007-2008_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"Mock AIME 1 2007-2008 Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_2007-2008_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"Mock AIME 1 2007-2008 Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a hr